{
  "requirement": "The `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to present each group to the user with its exact text, including any `{sites}` and `{violations}` queries, and with each design question the review returned, along with its options and the presenting agent's recommendation.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligation.** The requirement says the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to present each group to the user. The presentation has four parts:\n- the group's exact text;\n- any `{sites}` and `{violations}` queries;\n- each design question the review returned;\n- each question's options and the presenting agent's recommendation.\n\nThe requirement is about what the skill's text says, so the right test checks that text.\n\n**Test.** `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_presents_exact_text_and_design_questions]` carries `{test}` for the requirement. It calls `assert_phrases(\"habeas-requirements\", …)`. The helper builds `bundled_skill(name)` from the bundled `SKILL.md` and its references, and collapses whitespace with `collapse`. It then asserts `contains` for the phrase and panics with a message if the phrase is missing.\n\nThe phrase is: \"Present each group to the user: its exact text, including any `{sites}` and `{violations}` queries, and the design questions the review returned, each with its options and your recommendation\".\n\nCollapsing whitespace matters because the line-wrapped step 4 in `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` (`## Workflow`) then matches. I read that step and its text matches the asserted phrase.\n\n**Mapping.** One assertion covers every clause: exact text, the `{sites}` and `{violations}` queries, the design questions, the options, and the recommendation. The phrase is long and specific. Removing any clause, such as the queries or the recommendation, would fail the test, so a weakened skill would not pass. Other tests that use \"Present each group to the user\" only check step ordering. They are separate from this requirement.\n\n**Gaps.** I found none. The exemption and delegation categories do not apply, and nothing is acknowledged by a `{fixme}`.",
